    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Priority:</b><br/>
High</p>

<p><b>Epic Link:</b><br/>
Authentication Enhancements</p>

<hr />

<p><b>Description:</b><br/>
As a user, I want to log in using either Passkey or Single Sign-On (SSO), so that I can access my account more securely and conveniently without relying solely on email/password authentication.</p>

<p>Two new login options — <b>“Sign in using SSO”</b> and <b>“Sign in with Passkey”</b> — have been added to the login page alongside existing authentication methods. These options should function seamlessly and provide a smooth user experience across supported environments.</p>

<hr />

<p><b>Acceptance Criteria:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li><b>UI Visibility</b>
	<ul>
		<li>GIVEN the user is on the login page</li>
		<li>THEN the following buttons should be visible:
		<ul>
			<li>“Sign in using SSO”</li>
			<li>“Sign in with Passkey”</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li>AND they should be displayed below the “Sign in with Google” option</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li><b>SSO Login Flow</b>
	<ul>
		<li>GIVEN the user clicks on “Sign in using SSO”</li>
		<li>WHEN valid SSO credentials are provided</li>
		<li>THEN the user should be successfully authenticated and redirected to the dashboard</li>
		<li>AND appropriate error messages should be shown for invalid credentials</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li><b>Passkey Login Flow</b>
	<ul>
		<li>GIVEN the user clicks on “Sign in with Passkey”</li>
		<li>WHEN a registered passkey is available and verified</li>
		<li>THEN the user should be logged in successfully</li>
		<li>AND redirected to the dashboard</li>
		<li>AND if no passkey is available, a fallback or guidance message should be displayed</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li><b>Error Handling</b>
	<ul>
		<li>Proper error messages should be displayed for:
		<ul>
			<li>Failed SSO authentication</li>
			<li>Passkey authentication failure</li>
			<li>Unsupported browser/device for passkeys</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li><b>Compatibility</b>
	<ul>
		<li>Passkey login should work on supported browsers/devices only</li>
		<li>SSO should work across all configured identity providers</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li><b>Security</b>
	<ul>
		<li>All authentication flows must follow secure protocols (OAuth/SAML/WebAuthn)</li>
		<li>No sensitive data should be exposed in UI or network logs</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
</ol>


<hr />

<p><b>Out of Scope:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Passkey registration flow (covered in separate story)</li>
	<li>SSO provider configuration</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<p><b>Test Scenarios:</b></p>

<ol>
	<li>Verify both new buttons are visible and correctly positioned</li>
	<li>Validate successful login via SSO</li>
	<li>Validate failed SSO login with incorrect credentials</li>
	<li>Validate successful login via Passkey</li>
	<li>Validate behavior when no passkey is registered</li>
	<li>Validate behavior on unsupported browsers/devices</li>
	<li>Verify UI responsiveness and accessibility</li>
</ol>


<hr />

<p><b>Definition of Done:</b></p>

<ul>
	<li>Feature implemented and deployed to staging</li>
	<li>All acceptance criteria met</li>
	<li>QA sign-off completed</li>
	<li>No critical or high defects open</li>
	<li>Documentation updated</li>
</ul>


<hr />

<p>If you want, I can also generate <b>test cases, edge cases, or automation scenarios (Playwright/Cypress)</b> for this story.</p>
            <br/>
